an overlay needs a branch: the baseline is the file
  action=refused — the baseline is the file itself — make a branch to experiment on
making a branch, then overlaying the section below it
  action=branched
  action=overlay-began on sec-2
the overlay editor opened with the canonical text:
    |function score(t)
    |  return t * 100
    |end function
typing into it, for real
  action=overlay-saved
the selector marks it experimental:
    Baseline
  * Robust [experimental: 1 section(s)]
    +
comparing
    |Robust against the file:
    |  sec-2:
    |    1 line(s) unchanged above
    |    -   return t * 100
    |    +   return t * 1000
    |    1 line(s) unchanged below
running the branch
  target=<score is 500
>
the source editor still shows the FILE:
    |threshold = 0.5
    |
    |function score(t)
    |  return t * 100
    |end function
    |
    |print "score is " + score(threshold)
    |
promoting
  action=overlay-promoted — 1 section(s) — unsaved, as any edit is
and NOW the source editor shows it, as an unsaved edit:
    |threshold = 0.5
    |
    |function score(t)
    |  return t * 1000
    |end function
    |
    |print "score is " + score(threshold)
    |
app-exited
